  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Projections, flattenings, filters, concatenations, groupings and counts receive the changes of the queries they are built over through a registry of derived queries rather than through event handlers, so each costs one 48-byte subscription instead of up to six delegates and releasing it allocates nothing: building and disposing a seven-query chain over each of 256 one-element sources fell from 1,593 μs and 3,980 KB to 1,297 μs and 3,048 KB\nA query's derived queries now take each of its changes before any handler subscribed to its events hears of it, so a handler reading a derived query from within a change always finds it updated; previously this depended on whether the handler had subscribed before the derived query was built",
